WEBVTT

00:01:30.204 --> 00:01:33.663
Customers don't necessarily
trust HopSkip drivers --

00:01:33.704 --> 00:01:35.413
that would be relational trust.

00:01:35.454 --> 00:01:38.788
But they do trust
the HopSkipDrive system --

00:01:38.788 --> 00:01:41.204
what we call "systemic trust."

00:01:41.204 --> 00:01:42.913
And that's what makes it work.

00:01:43.954 --> 00:01:45.913
I am fascinated by this.

00:01:47.329 --> 00:01:48.496
Here in Brazil,

00:01:48.538 --> 00:01:51.788
people these days tend to say
that trust is a rare commodity.

00:01:51.788 --> 00:01:53.788
I don't think we are alone.

00:01:53.788 --> 00:01:57.038
Trust appears to have
broken down all around us.

00:01:57.079 --> 00:02:01.413
And yet, the concept of trust
has never been so fashionable.